1
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Scooby-Doo! and the Spooky Scarecrow is a animation,
family, mystery film directed by Michael Goguen.

2
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Scooby-Doo and the rest of the ghost-busting gang visit a quiet farm town where
everyone is preparing for the annual Halloween harvest celebration.

3
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Scooby-Doo / Fred Jones (voice), played by Frank Welker.

4
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Shaggy Rogers (voice), played by Matthew Lillard.

5
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Velma Dinkley (voice), played by Mindy Cohn.

6
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Daphne Blake (voice), played by Grey DeLisle.

7
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:06,000
Levi (voice), played by Josh Keaton.

8
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Sheriff Kern (voice), played by Wendie Malick.

9
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Scooby-Doo (often written as Scooby-Doo!) is an American
media franchise owned by Warner Bros.

10
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Entertainment and created in 1969 by writers Joe Ruby and Ken Spears through their animated series,
Scooby-Doo, Where Are You!, for Hanna-Barbera, which was later absorbed into Warner Bros.

11
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Animation in 2001.

12
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
The series features four teenagers named Fred Jones, Daphne Blake, Velma Dinkley, and Shaggy Rogers, and their talking Great Dane named Scooby-Doo, who solve mysteries
involving supposedly supernatural creatures through a series of antics and missteps, while traveling in a brightly colored van called the Mystery Machine.

13
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:06,000
The franchise has numerous shows, films, and specials.

14
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:06,000
Scooby-Doo was originally broadcast on CBS from
1969 to 1976, when it moved to ABC.

15
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,000
ABC aired various versions of Scooby-Doo until canceling it in 1986, and presented a spin-off
featuring the characters as children called A Pup Named Scooby-Doo from 1988 to 1991.

16
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Two Scooby-Doo reboots aired as part of Kids' WB on The WB
and its successor The CW from 2002 to 2008.

17
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:06,000
Further reboots aired on Cartoon Network from 2010 to 2018.

18
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
Repeats of the various Scooby-Doo series are frequently broadcast on Cartoon
Network's sister channel Boomerang in the United States and other countries.

19
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:06,000
The most recent Scooby-Doo series, Scooby-Doo and Guess Who?, premiered on June 27, 2019,
as an original series on Boomerang's streaming service and later HBO Max.

20
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
In 2013, TV Guide ranked Scooby-Doo the fifth-greatest TV cartoon of all time.

21
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:06,000
The film explores themes of farm, halloween, scarecrow, corn.

22
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:06,000
The tone is lighthearted and mind_bending.
